hexagon: format the profile line of an op when the host packs the batch

Base: llama.cpp commit c6824a9 plus every patch of the series before this one.

The defect

With GGML_HEXAGON_PROFILE the host writes one line for each op when the
response of the DSP comes. The line gives the names, the dims, the types and
the strides of the tensors of the op. The host read these values from the ggml
tensors at the time of the response. Before the response, llama.cpp can build
the next graph in the same memory, for example the graph of the next ubatch of
a prompt. Then the line shows the names and the dims of the next graph.

On the phone, the SCALE that clears the state cache_s showed the dims 0:1, but
its kernel params were for a full row of 2 MiB. Such lines gave incorrect byte
counts to the roofline analysis of tools/prof.

The change

The op batch makes the text of the line when it adds the op (add_op). When a
fusion changes the last op (try_fuse), the op batch makes the text again. The
batch keeps these texts in place of the op nodes, and the response adds the
times to them. A replay of the batch cache uses the texts of its snapshot.
Without the profile, the host makes no text. The format of the line does not
change.

The host does the same work as before, but at a different time. The times of
the ops come from the DSP and do not change.

The tests

hexhost_graphs (tests/fuzz/hexhost/graphs) ran the image turn of the 4B Q8_0
at 576 image tokens on the fake DSP, with GGML_HEXAGON_PROFILE=1 and
GGML_HEXAGON_VERBOSE=1. The image prompt needs more than one ubatch. A script
compared each profile line of an unfused op with the execute-op line that the
host wrote when it added the op:

- Without this patch, 6621 of 7761 lines differ. For example, an RMS_NORM
  shows the dims 128:16:28:1 in place of 128:16:512:1.
- With this patch, no line differs.

The decode path and the MTP path of hexhost_graphs give no difference with and
without this patch, because llama.cpp reads the logits before it builds the
next graph.

The test mode of tests/fuzz/hexhost gives 0 findings in the configurations
none, asan, ubsan, tsan and msan, each with the debug and the release profile.
The graph target sets the profile for one input of ten.

The phone

In the profile runs of the stage quick (a prompt of 1024 tokens in one ubatch,
then 8 decode tokens), the dims of each line agree with the op. That run has no
second ubatch, thus it does not show the defect.

